1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--uncorrected-reading-aloud","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/uncorrected-reading-aloud","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/uncorrected-reading-aloud","sourceHash":"0a1f9da542c6974b6825855c5ba2ddc49c12a02f404636bdd0d3c881d3af11ab","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:22.231Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Uncorrected Reading Aloud","zh":"未经纠正的朗读"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Reading aloud means finding a text in the target language and reading it out loud. \"Uncorrected\" means no one is giving you feedback — you're just practicing the physical act of speaking.","zh":"朗读是指找到一篇目标语言文本并大声读出来。“未经纠正”意味着没有人向你提供反馈——你只是在练习说话这一身体动作。"}},{"id":"why-it-helps","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Helps","zh":"为什么有帮助"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Reading aloud bridges the gap between knowing words and being able to say them. It trains your mouth, tongue, and jaw to form the sounds of the language, builds fluency of articulation, and helps you get comfortable with the physical sensation of speaking.","zh":"朗读弥合了认识词语与能够说出词语之间的差距。它训练你的嘴、舌头和下颌形成语言中的声音，提升发音流利度，并帮助你适应说话时的身体感受。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It's also low-pressure. You don't have to think about what to say (the text does that for you), so you can focus entirely on pronunciation and flow.","zh":"它的压力也很小。你不必思考要说什么（文本会替你完成这件事），因此可以把注意力完全放在发音和表达流畅度上。"}},{"id":"how-to-do-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Do It","zh":"操作方法"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Find a text in the target language (a book, article, or anything)","zh":"找到一篇目标语言文本（书籍、文章或任何其他内容）"},{"en":"Read it out loud at a comfortable pace","zh":"以舒适的速度大声朗读"},{"en":"If you stumble on a word, stop and repeat it. You can even redo a whole sentence or paragraph. <ul><li>You can also look up examples of how natives say that word with a tool like <a href=\"https://youglish.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">YouGlish</a></li></ul>","zh":"如果某个词读得磕绊，就停下来重复。你甚至可以重读整个句子或段落。<ul><li>你也可以使用<a href=\"https://youglish.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">YouGlish</a>等工具，查找母语者如何说出这个词的示例</li></ul>"},{"en":"Then keep reading!","zh":"然后继续读！"}]},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"提示"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Choose text at your reading level — you should understand what you're saying","zh":"选择符合你阅读水平的文本——你应该理解自己正在说什么"},{"en":"Different kinds of text can train different skills. Read a Wikipedia article if you want to practice saying numbers or dates. Read a play/subtitles if you want dialogue. Etc.","zh":"不同类型的文本可以训练不同技能。如果你想练习说数字或日期，可以读维基百科文章；如果你想练习对话，可以读剧本或字幕，等等。"},{"en":"You can optionally record yourself for later Speaking Analysis","zh":"你也可以选择录下自己的声音，以便之后进行口语分析"},{"en":"Even 10-15 minutes daily makes a noticeable difference in pronunciation confidence","zh":"每天即使只练习10—15分钟，也会明显提升你对发音的信心"},{"en":"Try reading aloud something you've written yourself (ideally after correction) for extra relevance","zh":"试着朗读自己写的内容（最好是在纠正之后），这样会更有针对性"}]},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Uncorrected reading aloud is introduced in Phase 4A and continues as a useful supplement through Phase 7.","zh":"未经纠正的朗读在阶段4A引入，并在阶段7之前持续作为一项有用的补充练习。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
